  "result": "I found the bug and wrote up a fix plan. I made no code changes because plan mode is active, and `ExitPlanMode` is unavailable in this session, so this message is the plan hand-off.\n\n**Cause:** `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py:750-754` returns `bound - dir`. The caller passes `dir=1` for the min bound and `dir=-1` for the max bound, so with open bounds it moves away from the valid range:\n- `min=0, min_open=True`, input `-5` clamps to `-1` instead of `1`.\n- `max=10, max_open=True`, input `15` clamps to `11` instead of `9`.\n\n**Fix:** change `return bound - dir` to `return bound + dir`.\n\n**Verification:**\n- Add tests in `tests/test_types.py` for open-bound clamped `IntRange`, asserting the result is inside the range.\n- Run `pytest tests/test_types.py tests/test_info_dict.py`.\n- Confirm `FloatRange._clamp` moves in the `dir` direction.\n\nThe plan is saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\some-users-report-that-ancient-ripple.md`. Tell me to proceed and I'll apply the fix and add the tests.",
